\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God's trumpet wakes the slumbering world:
\par Now each man to his post!
\par The red cross banner is unfurled:
\par Who joins the gracious host?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He who, in fealty  to the truth,
\par And counting all the cost,
\par Doth consecrate his generous youth-
\par He joins the noble host.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He who, no anger on his tongue,
\par Nor any idle boast,
\par Bears steadfast witness against wrong-
\par He joins the sacred host.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He who, with calm undaunted will,
\par Ne'er counts the battle lost,
\par But, though defeated, battles still-
\par He joins the faithful host.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. He who is ready for the cross,
\par The cause despised loves most,
\par And shuns not pain or shame or loss-
\par He joins the martyr host.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

